    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-14035",
      "problem": "Sketch the solution to the inequality ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/8ae7f874698e6a04fd7dc7dd9c542dfaf3083b8dcb697eb3a842ed64a65b796c.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "First, we draw the corresponding straight line ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/0357369787946460377c5ff4eed408338812c31faacdf61ffb230251c324e626.svg) Since the inequality involves a 'strictly greater than' sign, the line ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/4a6556bc87153b9f3ef528cc11325d373d44f659dbd4d66c1c3bdfaa7084f90e.svg) itself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a **dashed line.**\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/60af5fdbf308cd733c74ccdb655c8ce35bfb3f243cb1ed60ec1d754a6e7a52ca.png)\n\nThen, we must decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/64d1f8aa08301b53b131e34d718886396e8f667d0c7dd8193fadbf58502b306a.svg) refers to the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-values that are *greater than* those on the line ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/0a3c6070569f4c4bfa0778f3bb99d559040ff17d349cf67af83ad9ddf569f469.svg) so we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/62748c4bf08704e669ae4baf92b75a156c43db6835f7a095974c41e102d18072.png)\n\nLet's now check that we've shaded the correct part. First, we consider a point in the shaded region, say ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/779cec712506e0f798805963ab85841b46650fb22681d97a64aec4b85a47d07f.svg)  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/058ac314ff7752e62cf751f7462c2f22980915b7b7821ffc9f005149a99c11d7.png)\n\nWhen we substitute the coordinates of this point into our inequality, we get a true statement:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/384ccb666b2d9fb1b49e04d8152d8698747564b39e898e37fa5d638326bed13e.svg) \n\nThis indicates that we have shaded the correct region.",
